DevOps is a collaborative methodology that merges software development (Dev) and IT operations (Ops) to deliver applications and services faster, with higher quality, and more reliability. It focuses on continuous integration, continuous delivery (CI/CD), automation, and close collaboration between teams to shorten the software development lifecycle.
Core principles include:
Collaboration: Breaking down silos between development and operations.
Automation: Reducing manual work in building, testing, and deployment.
Continuous Feedback: Using monitoring and logging to improve processes.
Iterative Improvement: Adopting Agile-inspired cycles for rapid delivery.
Key Practices and Tools
CI/CD Pipelines: Tools like Jenkins, GitHub Actions, and GitLab CI automate build, test, and deployment.
Containerization: Docker ensures consistent environments; Kubernetes orchestrates containers at scale.
Infrastructure as Code (IaC): Terraform, Ansible, and CloudFormation manage infrastructure declaratively.
Monitoring & Logging: Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK Stack provide real-time insights.
Version Control: Git enables collaborative code management.
